    "summary": "- `GET /api/invoices` accepts `limit` (default 20, whole number 1–100) and `cursor`, and returns `{\"items\": [...], \"next_cursor\": \"...\"}` in creation order (created, then id). Invalid limit gives 400 `invalid_limit`; an unreadable cursor gives 400 `invalid_cursor`.\n- Paging is stable under concurrent inserts: no invoice is skipped or repeated across pages. `next_cursor` is set only when more items exist.\n- Checked by new tests covering page sizes, the last page, bad limit and cursor values, and insertion between page requests. `go build ./...`, `go test ./...` and `go vet ./...` pass, and ex\n...[truncated]",
